existing hankweave-docs repo, (3) whether old repo should be archived/deleted.\n    22→\n    23→## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Monorepo workspace setup not explained\n    24→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `package.json`\n    25→**Issue**: Agent added `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to package.json and corresponding changes to sync/release scripts, but plan doesn't explain monorepo structure, workspace dependencies, or how docs workspace relates to main package.\n    26→**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) monorepo structure and workspace purpose, (2) whether docs workspace has separate package.json/dependencies, (3) build/test implications for workspace setup.\n    27→\n    28→## [UNCLEAR INSTRUCTIONS]: Release script schema validation scope ambiguous\n    29→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `scripts/release.ts`\n    30→**Issue**: Release script now checks both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/` in validation, but plan doesn't clarify whether schema generation should output to both locations or if they should be kept in sync.\n    31→**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) single source of truth for schemas, (2) whether docs/public/schemas is generated or manually maintained, (3) validation expectations for release process.\n    32→\n    33→\n    34→---\n    35→\n    36→## [SKIPPED STEPS]: Baseline test output not reviewed before proceeding\n    37→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `test-output-20260305-135120.txt`\n    38→**Issue**: Agent marked \"Run baseline tests\" as completed but never actually read or analyzed the test output file that was initially attempted (event 1772718687836 showed read attempt with timeout error). Agent proceeded to verification without understanding baseline state.\n    39→**Fix**: Plan should require explicit step: read and document baseline test results before moving to verification phase. This establishes what was broken and what should be fixed.\n    40→\n    41→## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Docs workspace build requirements not specified\n    42→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `docs/package.json`\n    43→**Issue**: Agent is about to run `bun run build` in docs workspace but plan doesn't specify: (1) what build command should do, (2) expected output location, (3) whether build should succeed or is expected to fail, (4) dependencies on root package generation.\n    44→**Fix**: Plan should document: (1) docs build prerequisites (e.g., schemas must be generated first), (2) expected build artifacts, (3) success criteria for docs build verification.\n    45→\n    46→\n    47→---\n    48→\n    49→## [ENVIRONMENT ISSUES]: Next.js workspace root detection warning\n    50→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `docs/next.config.mjs`\n    51→**Issue**: Next.js build emits warning about multiple lockfiles and incorrect workspace root detection. It selected `/Users/philip/package-lock.json` instead of the bun monorepo root, though build succeeded despite the warning.\n    52→**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) add `outputFileTracingRoot` to Next.js config to explicitly set workspace root, or (2) document why this warning is acceptable and won't cause issues in CI/production builds.\n    53→\n    54→\n    55→---\n    56→\n    57→## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Pre-existing test failures not documented in plan\n    58→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts`\n    59→**Issue**: Agent states \"exactly the expected pre-existing 9 failures\" but plan never specified which tests should fail, how many, or why. Agent is making assumptions about what's \"expected\" without documented baseline.\n    60→**Fix**: Plan should include: (1) list of known failing tests with reasons, (2) which failures are acceptable/pre-existing vs. which indicate migration problems, (3) success criteria for test run (e.g., \"same 9 failures as before migration\").\n    61→\n    62→\n    63→---\n    64→\n    65→No actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified:\n    66→- Schema generation writes to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/` \n    67→- npm pack correctly excludes `docs/` directory\n    68→- Runtime build completes successfully\n    69→- All verification steps proceeding as expected\n    70→\n    71→\n    72→---\n    73→\n    74→## [DISCREPANCY]: Schema changes attributed to wrong source\n    75→**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`\n    76→**Issue**: Agent correctly identifies that the `showCosts` field addition in schema diff comes from a merged feature branch (`philipn/eng-213-hankweave_runtime_show_costs`), not from the docs migration. However, plan doesn't mention this pre-existing code change or explain why schema diffs should be expected/ignored during verification.\n    77→**Fix**: Plan should clarify: (1) whether schema changes from unrelated PRs are expected in the working directory, (2) how to distinguish migration-related changes from feature changes, (3) whether schema verification should baseline against a clean state first.\n    78→\n    79→\n    80→---\n    81→\n    82→No actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified all plan requirements:\n    83→- `package.json` has `workspaces: ['docs']`\n    84→- `tsconfig.json` excludes `docs/**/*`\n    85→- All script changes (release.ts, sync-public.ts, test-sync-local.ts, generate-schemas.ts) are in place\n    86→- SOP documentation updated with docs workspace details\n    87→- All verification checks passing\n    88→\n    89→\n    90→---\n    91→\n    92→No actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified:\n    93→- `.gitignore` has correct docs build output entries (`docs/.next/`, `docs/out/`, `docs/public/_pagefind/`)\n    94→- `sync-public.ts` correctly deletes `workspaces` field in `transformPackageJson()` function\n    95→- All sync-public transformations in place for public