ionally not updated.\n   157→**Fix**: Plan should clarify in Phase 3, Step 3.2: either (1) add a log line like `console.log(\"    removed field: workspaces\");` to the logging block, or (2) document that the logging was left as-is and the workspaces deletion is silent.\n   158→\n   159→\n   160→---\n   161→\n   162→No actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent is systematically preparing to make targeted edits to the plan based on review findings. Agent has identified 5 specific edits needed and is gathering exact text locations for surgical modifications.\n   163→\n   164→\n   165→---\n   166→\n   167→No actionable issues detected. Agent is successfully making targeted edits to the plan based on review findings. First edit (Phase 1, Step 1.5 - Next.js workspace root warning) completed successfully.\n   168→\n   169→\n   170→---\n   171→\n   172→No actionable issues detected. Agent is proceeding with second targeted edit to Phase 6, Step 6.2 to correct schema diff attribution.\n   173→\n   174→\n   175→---\n   176→\n   177→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed second edit (Phase 6, Step 6.2 - schema diff attribution correction) and is proceeding with third edit.\n   178→\n   179→\n   180→---\n   181→\n   182→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed third edit (Phase 6, Step 6.7 - release dry-run expected failure note).\n   183→\n   184→\n   185→---\n   186→\n   187→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed fourth edit (Summary of Changes table - schema diff description) and fifth edit (Phase 8, Step 8.1 - commit message schema diff note). Agent is proceeding with sixth and final edit.\n   188→\n   189→\n   190→---\n   191→\n   192→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed sixth and final edit (Phase 3, Step 3.2 - logging note for transformPackageJson). All targeted plan updates completed.\n   193→\n   194→\n   195→---\n   196→\n   197→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed seventh edit (Section g - schema generation output note) and is reviewing Section b (Information Available) to ensure consistency of schema diff description across all plan sections.\n   198→\n   199→\n   200→---\n   201→\n   202→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed eighth edit (Section b - Information Available summary) to ensure consistency of trial run findings across all plan sections.\n   203→\n   204→\n   205→---\n   206→\n   207→No actionable issues detected. Agent has completed all eight targeted plan edits and is now proceeding to write the final documentation of changes and reasoning.\n   208→\n   209→\n   210→---\n   211→\n   212→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed the plan update task by:\n   213→\n   214→1. Making 8 targeted edits to the plan based on implementation trial findings\n   215→2. Creating comprehensive documentation in `updation_thoughts_and_changes.md` explaining the reasoning behind each change\n   216→3. Correctly distinguishing between actual plan gaps (3 items: schema diff attribution, Next.js warning, release dry-run behavior) and sentinel observations that were already addressed in the plan\n   217→\n   218→The update task is complete.\n   219→\n   220→\n   221→---\n   222→\n   223→No actionable issues detected. Agent completed final verification pass confirming all 8 edits integrate cleanly with surrounding text and maintain document coherence. Plan update task is fully complete with all changes verified.\n   224→\n   225→\n   226→---\n   227→\n   228→No actionable issues detected. Agent successfully completed the entire plan update task:\n   229→\n   230→- 8 targeted edits made to plan.md based on implementation trial findings\n   231→- All edits verified for coherence and integration\n   232→- Comprehensive documentation created in updation_thoughts_and_changes.md\n   233→- All sentinel observations reviewed and appropriately handled (7 were already addressed in plan, 1 resulted in legitimate plan improvement)\n   234→\n   235→Task complete.\n   236→\n   237→\n   238→---\n   239→\n   240→No actionable issues detected. Agent is beginning a new task (final-step-compress) and exploring the plan directory structure to understand what artifacts need to be compressed/archived.\n   241→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"555a1c22-391a-4b03-8e05-f5f37fde42fb","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/implementations/current/sentinel-implementation-observations.md","content":"\n\n---\n\n## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Plan doesn't specify git state expectations\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: hankweave repository\n**Issue**: Agent discovers `docs/` directory already exists as untracked files with multiple modified files in git status (`.gitignore`, `bun.lock`, `package.json`, etc.). Plan doesn't clarify whether this is expected state or if a clean working directory was assumed.\n**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) expected git state before implementation starts, (2) whether to stash/commit existing changes, (3) whether `docs/` directory creation is idempotent or should skip if exists.\n\n## [ASSUMPTION VIOLATIONS]: Pre-existing docs directory conflicts with plan\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `/hankweave/docs/`\n**Issue**: `docs/` directory exists as untracked files (appears to be a Next.js documentation site with `app/`, `components/`, `content/`, etc.), but plan likely assumes creating docs from scratch. The directory structure suggests this isn't a fresh creation.\n**Fix**: Plan should clarify: (1) is this an existing docs site to be preserved/modified, or (2) should it be removed and recreated, or (3) should implementation skip if docs already exists?\n\n\n---\n\n## [DISCREPANCY]: Path change in generate-schemas.ts not documented\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `scripts/generate-schemas.ts`\n**Issue**: Diff shows path changed from `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site` to `docs`, but plan doesn't explain this architectural decision or whether the old external docs repo is being deprecated.\n**Fix**: Plan should document: (1) why moving from external repo to monorepo `docs/`, (2) migration strategy for existing hankweave-docs repo, (3) whether old repo should be archived/deleted.\n\n## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Monorepo workspace setup not explained\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `package.json`\n**Issue**: Agent added `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to package.json and corresponding changes to sync/release scripts, but plan doesn't explain monorepo structure, workspace dependencies, or how docs workspace relates to main package.\n**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) monorepo structure and workspace purpose, (2) whether docs workspace has separate package.json/dependencies, (3) build/test implications for workspace setup.\n\n## [UNCLEAR INSTRUCTIONS]: Release script schema validation scope ambiguous\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `scripts/release.ts`\n**Issue**: Release script now checks both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/` in validation, but plan doesn't clarify whether schema generation should output to both locations or if they should be kept in sync.\n**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) single source of truth for schemas, (2) whether docs/public/schemas is generated or manually maintained, (3) validation expectations for release process.\n\n\n---\n\n## [SKIPPED STEPS]: Baseline test output not reviewed before proceeding\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `test-output-20260305-135120.txt`\n**Issue**: Agent marked \"Run baseline tests\" as completed but never actually read or analyzed the test output file that was initially attempted (event 1772718687836 showed read attempt with timeout error). Agent proceeded to verification without understanding baseline state.\n**Fix**: Plan should require explicit step: read and document baseline test results before moving to verification phase. This establishes what was broken and what should be fixed.\n\n## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Docs workspace build requirements not specified\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `docs/package.json`\n**Issue**: Agent is about to run `bun run build` in docs workspace but plan doesn't specify: (1) what build command should do, (2) expected output location, (3) whether build should succeed or is expected to fail, (4) dependencies on root package generation.\n**Fix**: Plan should document: (1) docs build prerequisites (e.g., schemas must be generated first), (2) expected build artifacts, (3) success criteria for docs build verification.\n\n\n---\n\n## [ENVIRONMENT ISSUES]: Next.js workspace root detection warning\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `docs/next.config.mjs`\n**Issue**: Next.js build emits warning about multiple lockfiles and incorrect workspace root detection. It selected `/Users/philip/package-lock.json` instead of the bun monorepo root, though build succeeded despite the warning.\n**Fix**: Plan should specify: (1) add `outputFileTracingRoot` to Next.js config to explicitly set workspace root, or (2) document why this warning is acceptable and won't cause issues in CI/production builds.\n\n\n---\n\n## [MISSING CONTEXT]: Pre-existing test failures not documented in plan\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `tests/unit/codex-runtime-extractor.test.ts`\n**Issue**: Agent states \"exactly the expected pre-existing 9 failures\" but plan never specified which tests should fail, how many, or why. Agent is making assumptions about what's \"expected\" without documented baseline.\n**Fix**: Plan should include: (1) list of known failing tests with reasons, (2) which failures are acceptable/pre-existing vs. which indicate migration problems, (3) success criteria for test run (e.g., \"same 9 failures as before migration\").\n\n\n---\n\nNo actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified:\n- Schema generation writes to both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/` \n- npm pack correctly excludes `docs/` directory\n- Runtime build completes successfully\n- All verification steps proceeding as expected\n\n\n---\n\n## [DISCREPANCY]: Schema changes attributed to wrong source\n**Plan**: implement-loop-step-1-implement#2 | **File**: `schemas/hankweave.schema.json`\n**Issue**: Agent correctly identifies that the `showCosts` field addition in schema diff comes from a merged feature branch (`philipn/eng-213-hankweave_runtime_show_costs`), not from the docs migration. However, plan doesn't mention this pre-existing code change or explain why schema diffs should be expected/ignored during verification.\n**Fix**: Plan should clarify: (1) whether schema changes from unrelated PRs are expected in the working directory, (2) how to distinguish migration-related changes from feature changes, (3) whether schema verification should baseline against a clean state first.\n\n\n---\n\nNo actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified all plan requirements:\n- `package.json` has `workspaces: ['docs']`\n- `tsconfig.json` excludes `docs/**/*`\n- All script changes (release.ts, sync-public.ts, test-sync-local.ts, generate-schemas.ts) are in place\n- SOP documentation updated with docs workspace details\n- All verification checks passing\n\n\n---\n\nNo actionable issues detected in this batch. Agent successfully verified:\n- `.gitignore` has correct docs build output entries (`docs/.next/`