{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013Geh4SLDbY9G1djJ57te2M","type":"tool_result","content":"   815→\n   816→Optional: A lightweight monorepo smoke test could be added:\n   817→```typescript\n   818→// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\n   819→import { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\n   820→import * as fs from \"node:fs\";\n   821→import * as path from \"node:path\";\n   822→\n   823→describe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n   824→  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n   825→\n   826→  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n   827→    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n   828→    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n   829→  });\n   830→\n   831→  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n   832→    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n   833→  });\n   834→\n   835→  test(\"docs public directory exists\", () => {\n   836→    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\"))).toBe(true);\n   837→  });\n   838→});\n   839→```\n   840→\n   841→Note: An earlier version of this test checked `docs/public/schemas/` existence, but that directory is only created by `generate-schemas` and may not exist on a fresh checkout. The test now checks `docs/public/` instead, which is always present in the repo. If the team wants a schema-existence test, it should be in the schema generation test suite, not a structural smoke test.\n   842→\n   843→This is a small structural invariant check. Only add if the team wants structural tests.\n   844→\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"c7499cd4-d3ab-490a-8990-109e00155c9a","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/merged/plan.md","content":"\nOptional: A lightweight monorepo smoke test could be added:\n```typescript\n// tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\nimport { describe, test, expect } from \"bun:test\";\nimport * as fs from \"node:fs\";\nimport * as path from \"node:path\";\n\ndescribe(\"monorepo structure\", () => {\n  const ROOT = path.resolve(import.meta.dir, \"../..\");\n\n  test(\"root package.json declares docs workspace\", () => {\n    const pkg = JSON.parse(fs.readFileSync(path.join(ROOT, \"package.json\"), \"utf8\"));\n    expect(pkg.workspaces).toContain(\"docs\");\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs workspace has package.json\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"package.json\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n\n  test(\"docs public directory exists\", () => {\n    expect(fs.existsSync(path.join(ROOT, \"docs\", \"public\"))).toBe(true);\n  });\n});\n```\n\nNote: An earlier version of this test checked `docs/public/schemas/` existence, but that directory is only created by `generate-schemas` and may not exist on a fresh checkout. The test now checks `docs/public/` instead, which is always present in the repo. If the team wants a schema-existence test, it should be in the schema generation test suite, not a structural smoke test.\n\nThis is a small structural invariant check. Only add if the team wants structural tests.\n","numLines":30,"startLine":815,"totalLines":957}},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:07:36.827Z"}
