{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_014EdpDHRT9efy3rAgqkD3tK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Lrbj9NGYr1BUK6uv6qZx8U","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/human_briefing.md","content":"# Monorepo Migration Briefing\n\nFor a senior engineer reviewing the plan before implementation begins.\n\n---\n\n## What is this?\n\nWe are consolidating `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (the runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (the documentation site) into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime stays at the repo root. The docs move in as a workspace at `docs/`, flattened from the current `nextra-site/` subdirectory in the docs repo. The public mirror (`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime`) continues to exist as a separate repo and is unaffected beyond strip list updates.\n\nThe full plan is at `plan/merged/plan.md`. It has been through three rounds of review and two implementation trial runs against the source snapshot. All trial runs completed successfully and surfaced only pre-existing issues (the `bun-types` typecheck failure and the 9 Codex binary locator test failures), not regressions.\n\n---\n\n## Why now?\n\nThere is already a live cross-repo dependency: `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` reaches into `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/` to write schema JSON files. This only works when both repos are cloned as siblings. A monorepo makes this relationship explicit. The broader motivation is that cross-cutting changes (e.g., a runtime feature that also needs docs updates) currently require coordinating multiple PRs across repos.\n\n---\n\n## Scope of changes\n\nThis migration touches **~40 lines of code across 9 existing files**, plus adds the docs directory (~30 files). No runtime code under `server/`, `types/`, `shims/`, or `tests/` is modified. The changes are:\n\n| File | What changes |\n|------|-------------|\n| `package.json` | Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` after `\"engines\"` |\n| `tsconfig.json` | Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array |\n| `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path from sibling repo to `docs/public/schemas/` |\n| `scripts/sync-public.ts` | Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS`; add `delete pkg.workspaces` to `transformPackageJson()` |\n| `scripts/release.ts` | Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP`; extend schema diff check, revert, and git add to cover `docs/public/schemas/` |\n| `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | Add `--exclude='docs'` to rsync; add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` verification list |\n| `.gitignore` | Add `docs/.next/`, `docs/out/`, `docs/public/_pagefind/` |\n| `standard-operating-procedures.md` | Update repo structure diagram, strip list docs, key files, add docs workflow section |\n| `bun.lock` | Regenerated as unified workspace lockfile |\n\n---\n\n## Major decisions (already made in the plan, need your sign-off)\n\n### 1. Runtime stays at root, docs moves into `docs/`\n\nThe runtime has 8 scripts, 3 CI workflows, 3 composite actions, and extensive relative path usage (`import.meta.dir` + `\"..\"`, `server/utils.ts` reading `../package.json` for version metadata). Moving it into a subdirectory would be a large refactor. The docs site has no CI of its own and a single `package.json`. Moving the docs in is the minimal-disruption approach.\n\nThe alternative of putting both packages in `packages/` subdirectories was considered and rejected. It is the conventional monorepo layout but would require rewriting every path in every script and workflow for no real benefit with only two packages.\n\n### 2. Flatten `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/`\n\nThe docs repo has a wrapper level (`hankweave-docs/`) containing `notes/`, `plan/`, and `README.md` around the actual `nextra-site/` directory. In the monorepo, this wrapper serves no purpose. The workspace path `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` is cleaner than `\"workspaces\": [\"hankweave-docs/nextra-site\"]`. The wrapper's `notes/` and `plan/` are development artifacts and are discarded.\n\n### 3. No `workspace:*` dependency between docs and runtime\n\nThe docs site does not `import` anything from the runtime package. The only data flow is schema JSON files copied by `generate-schemas.ts`. This is a script-level file operation, not a package dependency. Adding `workspace:*` would incorrectly suggest the docs depend on the runtime as a library.\n\n### 4. No Turborepo\n\nTwo packages do not need task orchestration or build caching. Bun workspaces is sufficient. Turborepo can be added later if more packages are introduced or CI times become problematic.\n\n### 5. Strip `\"workspaces\"` from public `package.json`\n\nThe `transformPackageJson()` function in `sync-public.ts` must delete `pkg.workspaces` before writing the public `package.json`. Without this, the public mirror would ship a `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` key pointing to a directory that does not exist, which could cause issues when users run `bun install` or `npm install` on the public repo. This was the single most important finding from the Codex plan review.\n\n### 6. Simple file copy for docs (no git subtree)\n\nThe plan defaults to a simple file copy with a descriptive commit. Git history for the docs repo is \"nice to have\" but not critical — the original repo remains available as an archive. The git subtree method is documented as an optional escape hatch in the plan if you prefer history preservation.\n\n---\n\n## Judgement calls (where the plan took a position you may want to override)\n\n### A. Optional CHANGELOG entry\n\nThe plan suggests adding an entry under `[Unreleased] > Changed` noting the monorepo migration. Since this is an internal infrastructure change (not user-facing), this is optional. If you prefer to keep the CHANGELOG strictly user-facing, skip it.\n\n### B. Optional monorepo smoke test\n\nThe plan includes an optional `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` that validates the workspace config and docs directory existence. It is a small structural invariant check — only add if you want structural tests in the suite.\n\n### C. Optional docs build CI job\n\nThe plan recommends adding a `docs-build` job to `ci.yml` that runs `cd docs && bun run build`. Without it, a broken docs build would only be caught by Vercel deployment failures, not by PR CI checks. This adds ~1-2 minutes to CI runs. The plan presents it as \"recommended optional.\"\n\n### D. Optional schema generation CI check\n\nA CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and then `git diff --exit-code schemas/ docs/public/schemas/` to ensure schemas are committed in sync. Only needed if schema drift has been a historical problem.\n\n### E. Git history preservation method\n\nAs noted above, the default is a simple file copy. If you want full commit history from `hankweave-docs` preserved at the `docs/` prefix, the git subtree merge commands are documented in the plan (Section i). This adds complexity to the migration commit but preserves `git log -- docs/` history.\n\n---\n\n## Vercel configuration (requires manual action)\n\nThis cannot be automated. After the migration PR is merged and CI is green:\n\n1. Change the Vercel project's connected repo from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n2. Set Root Directory to `docs`. This is important — `docs/vercel.json` contains the `installCommand`, `buildCommand`, and the `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` build env flag. Vercel only picks up `vercel.json` at the configured Root Directory. If Root Directory were set to `/` instead, all of these settings would be silently ignored.\n3. Optionally set \"Ignored Build Step\" to `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/` to skip rebuilds when only runtime code changes.\n4. Configure production and preview deployment branches (likely `develop` for production, PRs for preview).\n\nThe `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag is being carried over verbatim from the existing docs repo. The implementing agent has been instructed not to proceed with Vercel configuration without explicit sign-off from whoever owns the docs deployment and knows why this flag exists.\n\n---\n\n## What the plan explicitly does NOT change\n\n- No runtime code (`server/`, `types/`, `shims/`)\n- No test files\n- No CI workflow files (they work as-is because the runtime stays at root)\n- No `biome.json` (its whitelist only covers runtime files; docs use their own tooling)\n- No `bunfig.toml`\n- No user-facing documentation (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`)\n- No public README or release files\n\n---\n\n## Known pre-existing issues (not caused by migration)\n\nThese exist on `develop` today and will still exist after migration:\n\n1. `bun run tc` fails — `tsconfig.json` references `bun-types` but the package is stored in a non-standard location. Separate fix needed.\n2. 9 unit tests fail — Codex binary locator tests that need `@openai/codex-sdk` installed.\n3. `bun run test:integration` script definition is broken — it runs `bun tests/integration` (file-run mode) instead of `bun test tests/integration` (test-run mode). Works when invoked directly as `bun test tests/integration`.\n\n---\n\n## Risk assessment\n\n**Low risk.** The migration changes zero runtime code. The most likely failure mode is the unified lockfile not working correctly with `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI — this is caught immediately and fixed by regenerating the lockfile. The Vercel deployment is the only part that requires careful manual configuration.\n\n---\n\n## How to review\n\nThe full plan with exact code snippets, line numbers, and step-by-step instructions is at `plan/merged/plan.md`. Supporting context:\n\n- `plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md` — docs site details and Vercel migration\n- `plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md` — test impact analysis and CI adjustments\n- `plan/task.md` — original task description and open questions\n- `plan/reviews/current/review.md` — most recent blind review of the plan\n- `plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md` — results from the implementation trial run\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":299,"cache_read_input_tokens":92354,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":299},"output_tokens":2663,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"dc8d4200-7608-4bc2-a00a-0663ca7717dd","timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:08:50.158Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Lrbj9NGYr1BUK6uv6qZx8U","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/human_briefing.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"8495da7c-2751-469c-8ebf-55dfd15c7afb","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/human_briefing.md","content":"# Monorepo Migration Briefing\n\nFor a senior engineer reviewing the plan before implementation begins.\n\n---\n\n## What is this?\n\nWe are consolidating `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave` (the runtime) and `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` (the documentation site) into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime stays at the repo root. The docs move in as a workspace at `docs/`, flattened from the current `nextra-site/` subdirectory in the docs repo. The public mirror (`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime`) continues to exist as a separate repo and is unaffected beyond strip list updates.\n\nThe full plan is at `plan/merged/plan.md`. It has been through three rounds of review and two implementation trial runs against the source snapshot. All trial runs completed successfully and surfaced only pre-existing issues (the `bun-types` typecheck failure and the 9 Codex binary locator test failures), not regressions.\n\n---\n\n## Why now?\n\nThere is already a live cross-repo dependency: `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` reaches into `../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas/` to write schema JSON files. This only works when both repos are cloned as siblings. A monorepo makes this relationship explicit. The broader motivation is that cross-cutting changes (e.g., a runtime feature that also needs docs updates) currently require coordinating multiple PRs across repos.\n\n---\n\n## Scope of changes\n\nThis migration touches **~40 lines of code across 9 existing files**, plus adds the docs directory (~30 files). No runtime code under `server/`, `types/`, `shims/`, or `tests/` is modified. The changes are:\n\n| File | What changes |\n|------|-------------|\n| `package.json` | Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` after `\"engines\"` |\n| `tsconfig.json` | Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array |\n| `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` | Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path from sibling repo to `docs/public/schemas/` |\n| `scripts/sync-public.ts` | Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS`; add `delete pkg.workspaces` to `transformPackageJson()` |\n| `scripts/release.ts` | Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP`; extend schema diff check, revert, and git add to cover `docs/public/schemas/` |\n| `scripts/test-sync-local.ts` | Add `--exclude='docs'` to rsync; add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` verification list |\n| `.gitignore` | Add `docs/.next/`, `docs/out/`, `docs/public/_pagefind/` |\n| `standard-operating-procedures.md` | Update repo structure diagram, strip list docs, key files, add docs workflow section |\n| `bun.lock` | Regenerated as unified workspace lockfile |\n\n---\n\n## Major decisions (already made in the plan, need your sign-off)\n\n### 1. Runtime stays at root, docs moves into `docs/`\n\nThe runtime has 8 scripts, 3 CI workflows, 3 composite actions, and extensive relative path usage (`import.meta.dir` + `\"..\"`, `server/utils.ts` reading `../package.json` for version metadata). Moving it into a subdirectory would be a large refactor. The docs site has no CI of its own and a single `package.json`. Moving the docs in is the minimal-disruption approach.\n\nThe alternative of putting both packages in `packages/` subdirectories was considered and rejected. It is the conventional monorepo layout but would require rewriting every path in every script and workflow for no real benefit with only two packages.\n\n### 2. Flatten `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/`\n\nThe docs repo has a wrapper level (`hankweave-docs/`) containing `notes/`, `plan/`, and `README.md` around the actual `nextra-site/` directory. In the monorepo, this wrapper serves no purpose. The workspace path `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` is cleaner than `\"workspaces\": [\"hankweave-docs/nextra-site\"]`. The wrapper's `notes/` and `plan/` are development artifacts and are discarded.\n\n### 3. No `workspace:*` dependency between docs and runtime\n\nThe docs site does not `import` anything from the runtime package. The only data flow is schema JSON files copied by `generate-schemas.ts`. This is a script-level file operation, not a package dependency. Adding `workspace:*` would incorrectly suggest the docs depend on the runtime as a library.\n\n### 4. No Turborepo\n\nTwo packages do not need task orchestration or build caching. Bun workspaces is sufficient. Turborepo can be added later if more packages are introduced or CI times become problematic.\n\n### 5. Strip `\"workspaces\"` from public `package.json`\n\nThe `transformPackageJson()` function in `sync-public.ts` must delete `pkg.workspaces` before writing the public `package.json`. Without this, the public mirror would ship a `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` key pointing to a directory that does not exist, which could cause issues when users run `bun install` or `npm install` on the public repo. This was the single most important finding from the Codex plan review.\n\n### 6. Simple file copy for docs (no git subtree)\n\nThe plan defaults to a simple file copy with a descriptive commit. Git history for the docs repo is \"nice to have\" but not critical — the original repo remains available as an archive. The git subtree method is documented as an optional escape hatch in the plan if you prefer history preservation.\n\n---\n\n## Judgement calls (where the plan took a position you may want to override)\n\n### A. Optional CHANGELOG entry\n\nThe plan suggests adding an entry under `[Unreleased] > Changed` noting the monorepo migration. Since this is an internal infrastructure change (not user-facing), this is optional. If you prefer to keep the CHANGELOG strictly user-facing, skip it.\n\n### B. Optional monorepo smoke test\n\nThe plan includes an optional `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` that validates the workspace config and docs directory existence. It is a small structural invariant check — only add if you want structural tests in the suite.\n\n### C. Optional docs build CI job\n\nThe plan recommends adding a `docs-build` job to `ci.yml` that runs `cd docs && bun run build`. Without it, a broken docs build would only be caught by Vercel deployment failures, not by PR CI checks. This adds ~1-2 minutes to CI runs. The plan presents it as \"recommended optional.\"\n\n### D. Optional schema generation CI check\n\nA CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and then `git diff --exit-code schemas/ docs/public/schemas/` to ensure schemas are committed in sync. Only needed if schema drift has been a historical problem.\n\n### E. Git history preservation method\n\nAs noted above, the default is a simple file copy. If you want full commit history from `hankweave-docs` preserved at the `docs/` prefix, the git subtree merge commands are documented in the plan (Section i). This adds complexity to the migration commit but preserves `git log -- docs/` history.\n\n---\n\n## Vercel configuration (requires manual action)\n\nThis cannot be automated. After the migration PR is merged and CI is green:\n\n1. Change the Vercel project's connected repo from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`.\n2. Set Root Directory to `docs`. This is important — `docs/vercel.json` contains the `installCommand`, `buildCommand`, and the `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` build env flag. Vercel only picks up `vercel.json` at the configured Root Directory. If Root Directory were set to `/` instead, all of these settings would be silently ignored.\n3. Optionally set \"Ignored Build Step\" to `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/` to skip rebuilds when only runtime code changes.\n4. Configure production and preview deployment branches (likely `develop` for production, PRs for preview).\n\nThe `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag is being carried over verbatim from the existing docs repo. The implementing agent has been instructed not to proceed with Vercel configuration without explicit sign-off from whoever owns the docs deployment and knows why this flag exists.\n\n---\n\n## What the plan explicitly does NOT change\n\n- No runtime code (`server/`, `types/`, `shims/`)\n- No test files\n- No CI workflow files (they work as-is because the runtime stays at root)\n- No `biome.json` (its whitelist only covers runtime files; docs use their own tooling)\n- No `bunfig.toml`\n- No user-facing documentation (`docs/content/**/*.mdx`)\n- No public README or release files\n\n---\n\n## Known pre-existing issues (not caused by migration)\n\nThese exist on `develop` today and will still exist after migration:\n\n1. `bun run tc` fails — `tsconfig.json` references `bun-types` but the package is stored in a non-standard location. Separate fix needed.\n2. 9 unit tests fail — Codex binary locator tests that need `@openai/codex-sdk` installed.\n3. `bun run test:integration` script definition is broken — it runs `bun tests/integration` (file-run mode) instead of `bun test tests/integration` (test-run mode). Works when invoked directly as `bun test tests/integration`.\n\n---\n\n## Risk assessment\n\n**Low risk.** The migration changes zero runtime code. The most likely failure mode is the unified lockfile not working correctly with `bun install --frozen-lockfile` in CI — this is caught immediately and fixed by regenerating the lockfile. The Vercel deployment is the only part that requires careful manual configuration.\n\n---\n\n## How to review\n\nThe full plan with exact code snippets, line numbers, and step-by-step instructions is at `plan/merged/plan.md`. Supporting context:\n\n- `plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md` — docs site details and Vercel migration\n- `plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md` — test impact analysis and CI adjustments\n- `plan/task.md` — original task description and open questions\n- `plan/reviews/current/review.md` — most recent blind review of the plan\n- `plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md` — results from the implementation trial run\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:08:50.800Z"}
