{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01YR6HiAGFgbxa27FXKog7iM","type":"tool_result","content":"Todos have been modified successfully. Ensure that you continue to use the todo list to track your progress. Please proceed with the current tasks if applicable"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"116b2d74-7409-4552-a18d-2abb654b7761","tool_use_result":{"oldTodos":[{"content":"Read and understand full plan and all addendums","status":"completed","activeForm":"Reading plan and addendums"},{"content":"Identify parts of plan needing compression or clarification","status":"completed","activeForm":"Identifying plan improvements"},{"content":"Make targeted edits to the plan if needed","status":"completed","activeForm":"Making targeted plan edits"},{"content":"Write plan/human_briefing.md for senior engineer review","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Writing human briefing"},{"content":"Write plan/drop_me_into_your_agent.md for implementing agent","status":"pending","activeForm":"Writing agent implementation guide"}],"newTodos":[{"content":"Read and understand full plan and all addendums","status":"completed","activeForm":"Reading plan and addendums"},{"content":"Identify parts of plan needing compression or clarification","status":"completed","activeForm":"Identifying plan improvements"},{"content":"Make targeted edits to the plan if needed","status":"completed","activeForm":"Making targeted plan edits"},{"content":"Write plan/human_briefing.md for senior engineer review","status":"completed","activeForm":"Writing human briefing"},{"content":"Write plan/drop_me_into_your_agent.md for implementing agent","status":"in_progress","activeForm":"Writing agent implementation guide"}]},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:08:58.205Z"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01Vci4GUGWqh6a7DK7Cgb92W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019JsaaVcNS4cR9VDS1NZQ7R","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/drop_me_into_your_agent.md","content":"# Monorepo Migration: Implementation Guide\n\nYou are implementing a monorepo migration for the Hankweave project. This document tells you where to find everything, what to do, and how to verify your work.\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Read These Files First\n\n**BEFORE YOU DO ANYTHING ELSE**, read these files into your context. They contain the full plan with exact code snippets, line numbers, and step-by-step instructions. Do not start implementation without reading them.\n\n1. **`plan/merged/plan.md`** — THE PRIMARY PLAN. Contains all 8 phases with exact code changes, line numbers, and verification steps. This is your source of truth.\n2. **`plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md`** — Details on the docs site structure, Vercel deployment, and schema flow.\n3. **`plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md`** — Test impact analysis and CI adjustment details.\n\nThese are supplementary and useful for understanding context but not required for implementation:\n- `plan/task.md` — Original task description and open questions that motivated the plan.\n- `plan/human_briefing.md` — Summary briefing written for a human reviewer. Good for quick orientation.\n- `plan/reviews/current/review.md` — The most recent blind review of the plan, with 18 numbered findings. All findings have been incorporated into the plan already.\n- `plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md` — Results from a trial implementation run. Confirms the plan works end-to-end.\n- `plan/review/current/updation_thoughts_and_changes.md` — Documents every edit made to the plan from review findings and the reasoning behind each.\n\n---\n\n## How this plan was developed\n\nThis plan went through multiple rounds of development:\n\n1. Two independent agents (Opus and Codex) each produced their own migration plan from the full source code.\n2. A review agent compared both plans, identified what each found that the other missed, and merged them into a single plan using Opus's structure with Codex's critical findings (especially the `transformPackageJson()` gap for stripping the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`).\n3. Three rounds of blind review were conducted, each by a fresh agent reading the plan and the source code. Each round surfaced corrections and improvements that were incorporated via targeted edits.\n4. Two implementation trial runs were executed against the source snapshot. Both completed all 8 phases successfully. The trial runs confirmed the plan's accuracy and surfaced only pre-existing issues (not regressions). Findings from the trials were incorporated back into the plan.\n\n**The trial implementations were discarded.** They were done against a source snapshot in a test environment to validate the plan, not as real implementation. You will be starting fresh from the tip of `develop`.\n\n---\n\n## About the project\n\nThe Hankweave project has three repos:\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`** (private) — The core TypeScript/Bun runtime. This is the repo you will be working in.\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`** (private) — The documentation site (Next.js + Nextra 4). You will copy its contents into `docs/` in the runtime repo.\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime`** (public) — Receives sanitized snapshots from the private repo. Not directly touched by this migration, but the sync scripts need updating to handle the new `docs/` directory.\n\nSource code snapshots are at:\n- `source/hankweave/` — The runtime repo\n- `source/hankweave-docs/` — The docs repo\n- `source/compiled-server-code.txt` — Frozen code snapshot (XML tagged, all together)\n- `source/compiled-docs.txt` — Compiled documentation\n- `source/compiled-tests-source.txt` — Compiled tests\n\nThe `standard-operating-procedures.md` in the runtime repo documents the branch model (`develop` -> `release/alpha`), the strip list conventions, and PR guidelines (squash merges).\n\n---\n\n## Step 0: Get informed consent from the human\n\nBefore you write any code, walk the human through the key decisions this plan makes and get their sign-off. The plan has already made these decisions, but the human needs to understand them and have the opportunity to change direction.\n\nPresent these decisions and ask for confirmation. If the human changes their mind on any, update `plan/merged/plan.md` with the revised approach before proceeding.\n\n### Critical decisions (must confirm)\n\n**Decision 1: Runtime stays at root, docs goes into `docs/`.**\nThe runtime has extensive relative path usage across 8 scripts, 3 CI workflows, and `server/utils.ts` (which reads `../package.json`). Moving the runtime into a subdirectory would require rewriting all of these. The docs site has no CI and a single `package.json`, so it is the thing that moves. The alternative (both packages in `packages/` subdirectories) was considered and rejected as excessive refactoring for two packages.\n\n**Decision 2: Flatten `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/`.**\nThe docs repo has a wrapper level containing `notes/`, `plan/`, and `README.md`. The plan discards these as development artifacts and flattens the `nextra-site/` contents directly into `docs/`. This gives a clean workspace path. The alternative (keeping the full nesting as `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`) was considered and rejected as unnecessarily deep.\n\n**Decision 3: Simple file copy, no git history preservation.**\nThe default approach copies files with a descriptive commit. The docs repo's git history is available in the original repo if needed. The git subtree method (which preserves full commit history at the `docs/` prefix) is documented in the plan as an optional alternative. Ask the human which they prefer.\n\n**Decision 4: Strip `\"workspaces\"` from public `package.json`.**\nThe `transformPackageJson()` function in `sync-public.ts` must delete the `workspaces` field so the public mirror does not ship a dangling reference to a `docs/` directory that does not exist there. This is a required change, not optional, but the human should know about it.\n\n### Optional items (ask the human which to include)\n\nPresent these as a checklist and ask which to do:\n\n1. **CHANGELOG entry** — Add an entry under `[Unreleased] > Changed` noting the monorepo migration. The plan marks this as optional since it is an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n\n2. **Monorepo smoke test** — A small `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` that validates the workspace config and docs directory existence. Only if the team wants structural tests.\n\n3. **Docs build CI job** — A new job in `ci.yml` that runs `cd docs && bun run build` to catch docs breakage from monorepo-level changes. Without it, broken docs are only caught by Vercel deployment failures.\n\n4. **Schema generation CI check** — A CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and verifies no uncommitted schema changes. Only needed if schema drift is a concern.\n\n5. **Vercel \"Ignored Build Step\"** — Configure `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/` to skip unnecessary docs rebuilds. Recommended but requires Vercel dashboard access.\n\nRecord the human's choices and proceed with only the items they approve.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Validate assumptions before starting\n\nBefore making any changes, verify these assumptions from the plan. If any fail, stop and reassess.\n\n```bash\n# You should be in the SouthBridgeAI/hankweave repo\n# Verify you're on develop and up to date\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit status  # Must be clean — no uncommitted changes\n\n# Verify key files exist at expected locations\nls package.json           # Root package.json must exist\nls tsconfig.json          # Root tsconfig must exist\nls scripts/generate-schemas.ts\nls scripts/sync-public.ts\nls scripts/release.ts\nls scripts/test-sync-local.ts\nls standard-operating-procedures.md\nls .gitignore\nls .github/workflows/ci.yml\n\n# Verify docs/ does NOT already exist\nls docs/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"WARNING: docs/ already exists — investigate before proceeding\"\n\n# Verify the generate-schemas.ts still has the old sibling-repo path\ngrep \"hankweave-docs\" scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n# Should show the old path: ../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas\n\n# Verify sync-public.ts STRIP_DIRS does NOT already include \"docs\"\ngrep \"STRIP_DIRS\" scripts/sync-public.ts\n# Should NOT contain \"docs\" yet\n\n# Verify release.ts INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP does NOT already include \"docs/\"\ngrep \"INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP\" scripts/release.ts -A 10\n# Should NOT contain \"docs/\" yet\n\n# Verify package.json does NOT already have \"workspaces\"\ngrep \"workspaces\" package.json\n# Should return nothing\n```\n\nIf any of these checks fail (e.g., `docs/` already exists, or `workspaces` is already in `package.json`), someone may have started this migration before. Investigate and decide whether to continue from their state or reset to clean `develop`.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Establish baseline\n\nRun the test suite before making any changes. Record the results to a file so you can compare later.\n\n```bash\n# Create a feature branch\ngit checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration\n\n# Run baseline checks and save output\nbun run lint 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-lint.txt\nbun run tc 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-tc.txt\nbun run test:unit 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-test-unit.txt\nbun test tests/integration 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-test-integration.txt\n```\n\n**Expected pre-existing failures (from the plan, Phase 0, Step 0.2):**\n- `bun run tc` fails with `TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'bun-types'`. This is a pre-existing tsconfig issue.\n- `bun run test:unit` shows approximately 1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail. The 9 failures are Codex binary locator tests.\n- `bun run lint` should pass cleanly.\n- `bun test tests/integration` should pass cleanly (~163 pass, 0 fail).\n\nRecord these numbers. After the migration, the same tests should produce the same results — no new failures.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Implement the migration\n\nFollow the plan's phases in order. The full details with exact code snippets and line numbers are in `plan/merged/plan.md`, Phases 1-5. Here is a condensed checklist:\n\n### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n\n- [ ] Copy `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/*` contents into `docs/` at the repo root. Do NOT copy the outer wrapper (`notes/`, `plan/`). You will need access to the docs repo or the source snapshot at `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`.\n- [ ] Delete `docs/bun.lock` (plain `rm`, not `git rm` — it was never committed).\n- [ ] Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to root `package.json` after `\"engines\"` and before `\"scripts\"`.\n- [ ] Run `bun install` from the repo root. Check output for warnings. The unified lockfile will be significantly larger (expected).\n- [ ] Verify docs build: `cd docs && bun run build && cd ..`\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n- [ ] Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in root `tsconfig.json`.\n- [ ] Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path in `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` (lines 24-32) from the sibling-repo path to `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\", \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\")`. Update the comment at line 75 about `docsAvailable`.\n- [ ] Run `bun run generate-schemas` and verify schemas appear in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\n### Phase 3: Update strip lists\n\n- [ ] `scripts/sync-public.ts`: Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS` (line 28).\n- [ ] `scripts/sync-public.ts`: Add `delete pkg.workspaces;` to `transformPackageJson()` between line 179 and line 181.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` (line 54).\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend schema diff check at line 427 to also cover `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend schema revert at line 436 to also cover `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend `git add` at line 510 to include `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`: Add `--exclude='docs'` to the rsync at line 80 (this is a TypeScript template literal, not bash).\n- [ ] `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`: Add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` array (line 160).\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The plan documents exact conventions for each script. `STRIP_DIRS` entries use bare names (`\"docs\"`), `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` entries use trailing slashes (`\"docs/\"`), and `shouldNotExist` entries use bare names (`\"docs\"`). Each script has its own `exec()` helper with a different signature — do not assume options from one exist in another. Read the plan's Phase 3 carefully for the exact edits.\n\n### Phase 4: Update `.gitignore`\n\n- [ ] Add `docs/.next/`, `docs/out/`, and `docs/public/_pagefind/` to the root `.gitignore`.\n\n### Phase 5: Update documentation\n\n- [ ] Update `standard-operating-procedures.md`: repo structure diagram (Section 1), strip list docs (what gets stripped section), key files reference (Section 9), add docs workflow subsection (Section 3), update the `package.json` transform description to mention `workspaces` removal.\n\nRead the plan's Phase 5 for the exact content to add. Be careful not to accidentally remove existing entries from the SOP's strip lists while editing.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Verify everything works\n\nRun through Phase 6 of the plan:\n\n```bash\n# Runtime checks (should match baseline — no new failures)\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\nbun run test:unit\nbun test tests/integration\n\n# Schema generation (should write to both locations)\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank.schema.json\nls docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json\n\n# Runtime build\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# Docs build\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n\n# npm pack (docs/ must NOT appear)\nnpm pack --dry-run\n\n# Sync dry-run (docs/ must be stripped, workspaces must be removed from package.json)\n# Use a version number — if the current version tag already exists on the public remote,\n# the script will fail at the tag step. Use a fake version like 999.0.0 if needed.\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version 999.0.0 --use-head\n# Then manually inspect /tmp/hankweave-sync-test/public/ to verify:\n#   - docs/ is absent\n#   - package.json has no \"workspaces\" field\n```\n\nAfter committing (next step), also run:\n```bash\n# Release dry-run (requires clean working tree — run AFTER committing)\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Implement optional items (per human's choices from Step 0)\n\nOnly do these if the human approved them:\n\n### CHANGELOG entry\nAdd under `[Unreleased] > Changed` in `CHANGELOG.md`:\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\n### Monorepo smoke test\nCreate `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` with the code from the plan's Section g.\n\n### Docs build CI job\nAdd the `docs-build` job to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` with the YAML from the plan's Section g.\n\n### Schema generation CI check\nAdd the schema verification step to CI with the YAML from the addendum-tests-and-ci.md, Section 5.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Run final verification and log output\n\nRun a comprehensive test suite and log it to a file for the record:\n\n```bash\nbun test 2>&1 | tee /tmp/final-test-output.txt\n```\n\nCompare the results against the baseline from Step 2. The pass/fail/skip counts should match. If there are new failures, investigate as regressions — stash your changes and re-run to confirm.\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Stage and commit\n\nStage changes carefully:\n\n```bash\n# Check what's changed\ngit status\ngit diff --stat\n\n# Stage all changes\ngit add docs/\ngit add package.json tsconfig.json bun.lock .gitignore\ngit add scripts/generate-schemas.ts scripts/sync-public.ts scripts/release.ts scripts/test-sync-local.ts\ngit add standard-operating-procedures.md\ngit add schemas/  # Include any schema diffs from regeneration\n\n# If CHANGELOG was updated:\ngit add CHANGELOG.md\n\n# If smoke test was added:\ngit add tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\n\n# If CI was updated:\ngit add .github/workflows/ci.yml\n\n# Review what's staged\ngit diff --cached --stat\n```\n\nCommit with:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nMigrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n- Include schema output diff (from dependency resolution and/or recent code changes)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nAfter committing, run the release dry-run (it requires a clean tree):\n```bash\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 8: Create PR\n\nPush and create a PR targeting `develop`:\n\n```bash\ngit push -u origin hrishi/monorepo-migration\n```\n\nPR title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n\nPR body should cover:\n- **Problem**: The hankweave and hankweave-docs repos have an implicit cross-repo dependency (`generate-schemas.ts` reaches into `../../hankweave-docs/`). Cross-cutting changes require coordinating multiple PRs.\n- **Solution**: Consolidate both repos into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime stays at root, docs moves into `docs/` as a workspace. Strip lists and sync scripts updated so the public mirror is unaffected.\n- **What changes**: List the files modified (the table from Step 3 above).\n- **What does NOT change**: No runtime code, no tests, no CI workflows (they work as-is), no user-facing docs.\n- **Verification**: All tests pass (same baseline), docs build succeeds, sync dry-run strips docs correctly, npm pack excludes docs.\n- **Manual follow-up needed**: Vercel project needs to be reconfigured to point at this repo with Root Directory set to `docs/`.\n\nNote: The repo uses squash merges, so the PR title becomes the commit message on `develop`. The bullet-point list in the commit message is for the feature branch record.\n\n---\n\n## Step 9: Update CHANGELOG.md\n\nIf not already done in Step 5, add a CHANGELOG entry. Even if the human said it was optional earlier, confirm with them one final time before the PR is merged. The entry goes under `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 10: Post-merge actions (out-of-band, document for the human)\n\nAfter the PR is merged and CI is green, these manual actions are needed:\n\n1. **Vercel reconfiguration** (Phase 7 of the plan):\n   - Change connected repo from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n   - Set Root Directory to `docs`\n   - Optionally set Ignored Build Step to `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n   - The `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag in `docs/vercel.json` is a human-approval gate — the team member who owns the docs Vercel deployment must confirm this flag is intentional\n\n2. **Archive old `hankweave-docs` repo** (only after Vercel is confirmed working from monorepo):\n   - Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (set to read-only)\n   - Update its README to say it has been merged into `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n   - Disconnect Vercel from the old repo\n\n---\n\n## Reminders\n\n- **Update plans if the user changes direction.** If the human overrides any decision in Step 0, edit `plan/merged/plan.md` to reflect the new approach before implementing.\n- **The trial implementations were discarded.** They were test runs to validate the plan. You are starting fresh from the tip of `develop`. Do not assume any migration work has already been done.\n- **Each script has its own conventions.** `STRIP_DIRS` uses bare names, `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` uses trailing slashes, `shouldNotExist` uses bare names. Each script has its own `exec()` helper with different signatures. Read the plan's Section d carefully.\n- **The plan has exact line numbers.** Use them as guides, but verify against the actual code — line numbers may have shifted if other PRs have been merged to `develop` since the plan was written.\n- **Do not over-engineer.** The plan is deliberately minimal. Do not add Turborepo, shared tsconfig, workspace link scripts, or monorepo orchestration tooling. The right amount of complexity is the minimum needed for the current task.\n\n---\n\n## Full TODO checklist\n\nFor easy tracking:\n\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/plan.md` (THE PRIMARY PLAN)\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md`\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md`\n- [ ] Present key decisions to human and get sign-off (Step 0)\n- [ ] Ask human about optional items (CHANGELOG, smoke test, CI jobs)\n- [ ] Update plan if human changes any decisions\n- [ ] Validate assumptions (Step 1)\n- [ ] Establish test baseline and save to file (Step 2)\n- [ ] Phase 1: Copy docs, add workspace config, run bun install, verify docs build\n- [ ] Phase 2: Update tsconfig exclude, update generate-schemas.ts path, verify schema generation\n- [ ] Phase 3: Update all strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- [ ] Phase 4: Update .gitignore\n- [ ] Phase 5: Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n- [ ] Verify all checks pass (Step 4)\n- [ ] Implement approved optional items (Step 5)\n- [ ] Run `bun test` and log to file (Step 6)\n- [ ] Stage changes and commit (Step 7)\n- [ ] Run release dry-run post-commit (Step 7)\n- [ ] Push and create PR (Step 8)\n- [ ] Update CHANGELOG.md (Step 9)\n- [ ] Document post-merge actions for the human (Step 10)\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":279,"cache_read_input_tokens":95364,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":279},"output_tokens":6131,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"747eb54d-3017-417c-bea0-ef2d6ffec6d6","timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:10:59.498Z"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019JsaaVcNS4cR9VDS1NZQ7R","type":"tool_result","content":"File created successfully at: /Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/drop_me_into_your_agent.md"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e33b59be-72d7-4a19-aa89-61c13bd6916e","uuid":"a51e6671-95cc-48cf-a863-58402fdb6111","tool_use_result":{"type":"create","filePath":"/Users/philip/projects/hw-budget-tests/plan-gen-execution/agentRoot/plan/drop_me_into_your_agent.md","content":"# Monorepo Migration: Implementation Guide\n\nYou are implementing a monorepo migration for the Hankweave project. This document tells you where to find everything, what to do, and how to verify your work.\n\n---\n\n## CRITICAL: Read These Files First\n\n**BEFORE YOU DO ANYTHING ELSE**, read these files into your context. They contain the full plan with exact code snippets, line numbers, and step-by-step instructions. Do not start implementation without reading them.\n\n1. **`plan/merged/plan.md`** — THE PRIMARY PLAN. Contains all 8 phases with exact code changes, line numbers, and verification steps. This is your source of truth.\n2. **`plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md`** — Details on the docs site structure, Vercel deployment, and schema flow.\n3. **`plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md`** — Test impact analysis and CI adjustment details.\n\nThese are supplementary and useful for understanding context but not required for implementation:\n- `plan/task.md` — Original task description and open questions that motivated the plan.\n- `plan/human_briefing.md` — Summary briefing written for a human reviewer. Good for quick orientation.\n- `plan/reviews/current/review.md` — The most recent blind review of the plan, with 18 numbered findings. All findings have been incorporated into the plan already.\n- `plan/implementations/current/implementation_issues.md` — Results from a trial implementation run. Confirms the plan works end-to-end.\n- `plan/review/current/updation_thoughts_and_changes.md` — Documents every edit made to the plan from review findings and the reasoning behind each.\n\n---\n\n## How this plan was developed\n\nThis plan went through multiple rounds of development:\n\n1. Two independent agents (Opus and Codex) each produced their own migration plan from the full source code.\n2. A review agent compared both plans, identified what each found that the other missed, and merged them into a single plan using Opus's structure with Codex's critical findings (especially the `transformPackageJson()` gap for stripping the `\"workspaces\"` field from the public `package.json`).\n3. Three rounds of blind review were conducted, each by a fresh agent reading the plan and the source code. Each round surfaced corrections and improvements that were incorporated via targeted edits.\n4. Two implementation trial runs were executed against the source snapshot. Both completed all 8 phases successfully. The trial runs confirmed the plan's accuracy and surfaced only pre-existing issues (not regressions). Findings from the trials were incorporated back into the plan.\n\n**The trial implementations were discarded.** They were done against a source snapshot in a test environment to validate the plan, not as real implementation. You will be starting fresh from the tip of `develop`.\n\n---\n\n## About the project\n\nThe Hankweave project has three repos:\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`** (private) — The core TypeScript/Bun runtime. This is the repo you will be working in.\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs`** (private) — The documentation site (Next.js + Nextra 4). You will copy its contents into `docs/` in the runtime repo.\n- **`SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-runtime`** (public) — Receives sanitized snapshots from the private repo. Not directly touched by this migration, but the sync scripts need updating to handle the new `docs/` directory.\n\nSource code snapshots are at:\n- `source/hankweave/` — The runtime repo\n- `source/hankweave-docs/` — The docs repo\n- `source/compiled-server-code.txt` — Frozen code snapshot (XML tagged, all together)\n- `source/compiled-docs.txt` — Compiled documentation\n- `source/compiled-tests-source.txt` — Compiled tests\n\nThe `standard-operating-procedures.md` in the runtime repo documents the branch model (`develop` -> `release/alpha`), the strip list conventions, and PR guidelines (squash merges).\n\n---\n\n## Step 0: Get informed consent from the human\n\nBefore you write any code, walk the human through the key decisions this plan makes and get their sign-off. The plan has already made these decisions, but the human needs to understand them and have the opportunity to change direction.\n\nPresent these decisions and ask for confirmation. If the human changes their mind on any, update `plan/merged/plan.md` with the revised approach before proceeding.\n\n### Critical decisions (must confirm)\n\n**Decision 1: Runtime stays at root, docs goes into `docs/`.**\nThe runtime has extensive relative path usage across 8 scripts, 3 CI workflows, and `server/utils.ts` (which reads `../package.json`). Moving the runtime into a subdirectory would require rewriting all of these. The docs site has no CI and a single `package.json`, so it is the thing that moves. The alternative (both packages in `packages/` subdirectories) was considered and rejected as excessive refactoring for two packages.\n\n**Decision 2: Flatten `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/` into `docs/`.**\nThe docs repo has a wrapper level containing `notes/`, `plan/`, and `README.md`. The plan discards these as development artifacts and flattens the `nextra-site/` contents directly into `docs/`. This gives a clean workspace path. The alternative (keeping the full nesting as `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`) was considered and rejected as unnecessarily deep.\n\n**Decision 3: Simple file copy, no git history preservation.**\nThe default approach copies files with a descriptive commit. The docs repo's git history is available in the original repo if needed. The git subtree method (which preserves full commit history at the `docs/` prefix) is documented in the plan as an optional alternative. Ask the human which they prefer.\n\n**Decision 4: Strip `\"workspaces\"` from public `package.json`.**\nThe `transformPackageJson()` function in `sync-public.ts` must delete the `workspaces` field so the public mirror does not ship a dangling reference to a `docs/` directory that does not exist there. This is a required change, not optional, but the human should know about it.\n\n### Optional items (ask the human which to include)\n\nPresent these as a checklist and ask which to do:\n\n1. **CHANGELOG entry** — Add an entry under `[Unreleased] > Changed` noting the monorepo migration. The plan marks this as optional since it is an internal infrastructure change, not user-facing.\n\n2. **Monorepo smoke test** — A small `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` that validates the workspace config and docs directory existence. Only if the team wants structural tests.\n\n3. **Docs build CI job** — A new job in `ci.yml` that runs `cd docs && bun run build` to catch docs breakage from monorepo-level changes. Without it, broken docs are only caught by Vercel deployment failures.\n\n4. **Schema generation CI check** — A CI step that runs `bun run generate-schemas` and verifies no uncommitted schema changes. Only needed if schema drift is a concern.\n\n5. **Vercel \"Ignored Build Step\"** — Configure `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/` to skip unnecessary docs rebuilds. Recommended but requires Vercel dashboard access.\n\nRecord the human's choices and proceed with only the items they approve.\n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Validate assumptions before starting\n\nBefore making any changes, verify these assumptions from the plan. If any fail, stop and reassess.\n\n```bash\n# You should be in the SouthBridgeAI/hankweave repo\n# Verify you're on develop and up to date\ngit checkout develop\ngit pull origin develop\ngit status  # Must be clean — no uncommitted changes\n\n# Verify key files exist at expected locations\nls package.json           # Root package.json must exist\nls tsconfig.json          # Root tsconfig must exist\nls scripts/generate-schemas.ts\nls scripts/sync-public.ts\nls scripts/release.ts\nls scripts/test-sync-local.ts\nls standard-operating-procedures.md\nls .gitignore\nls .github/workflows/ci.yml\n\n# Verify docs/ does NOT already exist\nls docs/ 2>/dev/null && echo \"WARNING: docs/ already exists — investigate before proceeding\"\n\n# Verify the generate-schemas.ts still has the old sibling-repo path\ngrep \"hankweave-docs\" scripts/generate-schemas.ts\n# Should show the old path: ../../hankweave-docs/nextra-site/public/schemas\n\n# Verify sync-public.ts STRIP_DIRS does NOT already include \"docs\"\ngrep \"STRIP_DIRS\" scripts/sync-public.ts\n# Should NOT contain \"docs\" yet\n\n# Verify release.ts INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP does NOT already include \"docs/\"\ngrep \"INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP\" scripts/release.ts -A 10\n# Should NOT contain \"docs/\" yet\n\n# Verify package.json does NOT already have \"workspaces\"\ngrep \"workspaces\" package.json\n# Should return nothing\n```\n\nIf any of these checks fail (e.g., `docs/` already exists, or `workspaces` is already in `package.json`), someone may have started this migration before. Investigate and decide whether to continue from their state or reset to clean `develop`.\n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Establish baseline\n\nRun the test suite before making any changes. Record the results to a file so you can compare later.\n\n```bash\n# Create a feature branch\ngit checkout -b hrishi/monorepo-migration\n\n# Run baseline checks and save output\nbun run lint 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-lint.txt\nbun run tc 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-tc.txt\nbun run test:unit 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-test-unit.txt\nbun test tests/integration 2>&1 | tee /tmp/baseline-test-integration.txt\n```\n\n**Expected pre-existing failures (from the plan, Phase 0, Step 0.2):**\n- `bun run tc` fails with `TS2688: Cannot find type definition file for 'bun-types'`. This is a pre-existing tsconfig issue.\n- `bun run test:unit` shows approximately 1512 pass, 4 skip, 9 fail. The 9 failures are Codex binary locator tests.\n- `bun run lint` should pass cleanly.\n- `bun test tests/integration` should pass cleanly (~163 pass, 0 fail).\n\nRecord these numbers. After the migration, the same tests should produce the same results — no new failures.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Implement the migration\n\nFollow the plan's phases in order. The full details with exact code snippets and line numbers are in `plan/merged/plan.md`, Phases 1-5. Here is a condensed checklist:\n\n### Phase 1: Bring docs into the repo\n\n- [ ] Copy `hankweave-docs/nextra-site/*` contents into `docs/` at the repo root. Do NOT copy the outer wrapper (`notes/`, `plan/`). You will need access to the docs repo or the source snapshot at `source/hankweave-docs/nextra-site/`.\n- [ ] Delete `docs/bun.lock` (plain `rm`, not `git rm` — it was never committed).\n- [ ] Add `\"workspaces\": [\"docs\"]` to root `package.json` after `\"engines\"` and before `\"scripts\"`.\n- [ ] Run `bun install` from the repo root. Check output for warnings. The unified lockfile will be significantly larger (expected).\n- [ ] Verify docs build: `cd docs && bun run build && cd ..`\n\n### Phase 2: Update cross-repo references\n\n- [ ] Add `\"docs/**/*\"` to the `exclude` array in root `tsconfig.json`.\n- [ ] Update `DOCS_SCHEMA_DIR` path in `scripts/generate-schemas.ts` (lines 24-32) from the sibling-repo path to `path.join(import.meta.dir, \"..\", \"docs\", \"public\", \"schemas\")`. Update the comment at line 75 about `docsAvailable`.\n- [ ] Run `bun run generate-schemas` and verify schemas appear in both `schemas/` and `docs/public/schemas/`.\n\n### Phase 3: Update strip lists\n\n- [ ] `scripts/sync-public.ts`: Add `\"docs\"` to `STRIP_DIRS` (line 28).\n- [ ] `scripts/sync-public.ts`: Add `delete pkg.workspaces;` to `transformPackageJson()` between line 179 and line 181.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Add `\"docs/\"` to `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` (line 54).\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend schema diff check at line 427 to also cover `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend schema revert at line 436 to also cover `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/release.ts`: Extend `git add` at line 510 to include `docs/public/schemas/`.\n- [ ] `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`: Add `--exclude='docs'` to the rsync at line 80 (this is a TypeScript template literal, not bash).\n- [ ] `scripts/test-sync-local.ts`: Add `\"docs\"` to `shouldNotExist` array (line 160).\n\n**IMPORTANT**: The plan documents exact conventions for each script. `STRIP_DIRS` entries use bare names (`\"docs\"`), `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` entries use trailing slashes (`\"docs/\"`), and `shouldNotExist` entries use bare names (`\"docs\"`). Each script has its own `exec()` helper with a different signature — do not assume options from one exist in another. Read the plan's Phase 3 carefully for the exact edits.\n\n### Phase 4: Update `.gitignore`\n\n- [ ] Add `docs/.next/`, `docs/out/`, and `docs/public/_pagefind/` to the root `.gitignore`.\n\n### Phase 5: Update documentation\n\n- [ ] Update `standard-operating-procedures.md`: repo structure diagram (Section 1), strip list docs (what gets stripped section), key files reference (Section 9), add docs workflow subsection (Section 3), update the `package.json` transform description to mention `workspaces` removal.\n\nRead the plan's Phase 5 for the exact content to add. Be careful not to accidentally remove existing entries from the SOP's strip lists while editing.\n\n---\n\n## Step 4: Verify everything works\n\nRun through Phase 6 of the plan:\n\n```bash\n# Runtime checks (should match baseline — no new failures)\nbun run lint\nbun run tc\nbun run test:unit\nbun test tests/integration\n\n# Schema generation (should write to both locations)\nbun run generate-schemas\nls schemas/hank.schema.json\nls docs/public/schemas/hank.schema.json\n\n# Runtime build\nbun run build\nls dist/index.js\n\n# Docs build\ncd docs && bun run build && cd ..\n\n# npm pack (docs/ must NOT appear)\nnpm pack --dry-run\n\n# Sync dry-run (docs/ must be stripped, workspaces must be removed from package.json)\n# Use a version number — if the current version tag already exists on the public remote,\n# the script will fail at the tag step. Use a fake version like 999.0.0 if needed.\nbun scripts/test-sync-local.ts --version 999.0.0 --use-head\n# Then manually inspect /tmp/hankweave-sync-test/public/ to verify:\n#   - docs/ is absent\n#   - package.json has no \"workspaces\" field\n```\n\nAfter committing (next step), also run:\n```bash\n# Release dry-run (requires clean working tree — run AFTER committing)\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 5: Implement optional items (per human's choices from Step 0)\n\nOnly do these if the human approved them:\n\n### CHANGELOG entry\nAdd under `[Unreleased] > Changed` in `CHANGELOG.md`:\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\n### Monorepo smoke test\nCreate `tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts` with the code from the plan's Section g.\n\n### Docs build CI job\nAdd the `docs-build` job to `.github/workflows/ci.yml` with the YAML from the plan's Section g.\n\n### Schema generation CI check\nAdd the schema verification step to CI with the YAML from the addendum-tests-and-ci.md, Section 5.\n\n---\n\n## Step 6: Run final verification and log output\n\nRun a comprehensive test suite and log it to a file for the record:\n\n```bash\nbun test 2>&1 | tee /tmp/final-test-output.txt\n```\n\nCompare the results against the baseline from Step 2. The pass/fail/skip counts should match. If there are new failures, investigate as regressions — stash your changes and re-run to confirm.\n\n---\n\n## Step 7: Stage and commit\n\nStage changes carefully:\n\n```bash\n# Check what's changed\ngit status\ngit diff --stat\n\n# Stage all changes\ngit add docs/\ngit add package.json tsconfig.json bun.lock .gitignore\ngit add scripts/generate-schemas.ts scripts/sync-public.ts scripts/release.ts scripts/test-sync-local.ts\ngit add standard-operating-procedures.md\ngit add schemas/  # Include any schema diffs from regeneration\n\n# If CHANGELOG was updated:\ngit add CHANGELOG.md\n\n# If smoke test was added:\ngit add tests/unit/monorepo-structure.test.ts\n\n# If CI was updated:\ngit add .github/workflows/ci.yml\n\n# Review what's staged\ngit diff --cached --stat\n```\n\nCommit with:\n```bash\ngit commit -m \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nMigrate to monorepo: bring docs into workspace\n\n- Add docs/ workspace (formerly SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs)\n- Add \"workspaces\" field to root package.json\n- Regenerate bun.lock as unified workspace lockfile\n- Exclude docs/**/* from root tsconfig.json\n- Update generate-schemas.ts to use monorepo-local docs path\n- Add docs/ to strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- Strip \"workspaces\" from public package.json in transformPackageJson()\n- Update release.ts schema handling for docs/public/schemas/\n- Add --exclude='docs' to test-sync-local.ts rsync\n- Update .gitignore for docs build artifacts\n- Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n- Include schema output diff (from dependency resolution and/or recent code changes)\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\nEOF\n)\"\n```\n\nAfter committing, run the release dry-run (it requires a clean tree):\n```bash\nbun scripts/release.ts patch --dry-run --skip-checks\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 8: Create PR\n\nPush and create a PR targeting `develop`:\n\n```bash\ngit push -u origin hrishi/monorepo-migration\n```\n\nPR title: `Monorepo migration: consolidate hankweave-docs into workspace`\n\nPR body should cover:\n- **Problem**: The hankweave and hankweave-docs repos have an implicit cross-repo dependency (`generate-schemas.ts` reaches into `../../hankweave-docs/`). Cross-cutting changes require coordinating multiple PRs.\n- **Solution**: Consolidate both repos into a single monorepo using Bun workspaces. The runtime stays at root, docs moves into `docs/` as a workspace. Strip lists and sync scripts updated so the public mirror is unaffected.\n- **What changes**: List the files modified (the table from Step 3 above).\n- **What does NOT change**: No runtime code, no tests, no CI workflows (they work as-is), no user-facing docs.\n- **Verification**: All tests pass (same baseline), docs build succeeds, sync dry-run strips docs correctly, npm pack excludes docs.\n- **Manual follow-up needed**: Vercel project needs to be reconfigured to point at this repo with Root Directory set to `docs/`.\n\nNote: The repo uses squash merges, so the PR title becomes the commit message on `develop`. The bullet-point list in the commit message is for the feature branch record.\n\n---\n\n## Step 9: Update CHANGELOG.md\n\nIf not already done in Step 5, add a CHANGELOG entry. Even if the human said it was optional earlier, confirm with them one final time before the PR is merged. The entry goes under `[Unreleased] > Changed`:\n\n```markdown\n- **Monorepo migration** -- Consolidated documentation site into the development repository as a Bun workspace. No changes to runtime behavior or public-facing interfaces.\n```\n\n---\n\n## Step 10: Post-merge actions (out-of-band, document for the human)\n\nAfter the PR is merged and CI is green, these manual actions are needed:\n\n1. **Vercel reconfiguration** (Phase 7 of the plan):\n   - Change connected repo from `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` to `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n   - Set Root Directory to `docs`\n   - Optionally set Ignored Build Step to `git diff --quiet HEAD^ HEAD -- docs/`\n   - The `DANGEROUSLY_DEPLOY_VULNERABLE_CVE_2026_0969` flag in `docs/vercel.json` is a human-approval gate — the team member who owns the docs Vercel deployment must confirm this flag is intentional\n\n2. **Archive old `hankweave-docs` repo** (only after Vercel is confirmed working from monorepo):\n   - Archive `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave-docs` on GitHub (set to read-only)\n   - Update its README to say it has been merged into `SouthBridgeAI/hankweave`\n   - Disconnect Vercel from the old repo\n\n---\n\n## Reminders\n\n- **Update plans if the user changes direction.** If the human overrides any decision in Step 0, edit `plan/merged/plan.md` to reflect the new approach before implementing.\n- **The trial implementations were discarded.** They were test runs to validate the plan. You are starting fresh from the tip of `develop`. Do not assume any migration work has already been done.\n- **Each script has its own conventions.** `STRIP_DIRS` uses bare names, `INTERNAL_FILES_TO_STRIP` uses trailing slashes, `shouldNotExist` uses bare names. Each script has its own `exec()` helper with different signatures. Read the plan's Section d carefully.\n- **The plan has exact line numbers.** Use them as guides, but verify against the actual code — line numbers may have shifted if other PRs have been merged to `develop` since the plan was written.\n- **Do not over-engineer.** The plan is deliberately minimal. Do not add Turborepo, shared tsconfig, workspace link scripts, or monorepo orchestration tooling. The right amount of complexity is the minimum needed for the current task.\n\n---\n\n## Full TODO checklist\n\nFor easy tracking:\n\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/plan.md` (THE PRIMARY PLAN)\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/addendum-docs-and-deployment.md`\n- [ ] Read `plan/merged/addendum-tests-and-ci.md`\n- [ ] Present key decisions to human and get sign-off (Step 0)\n- [ ] Ask human about optional items (CHANGELOG, smoke test, CI jobs)\n- [ ] Update plan if human changes any decisions\n- [ ] Validate assumptions (Step 1)\n- [ ] Establish test baseline and save to file (Step 2)\n- [ ] Phase 1: Copy docs, add workspace config, run bun install, verify docs build\n- [ ] Phase 2: Update tsconfig exclude, update generate-schemas.ts path, verify schema generation\n- [ ] Phase 3: Update all strip lists (sync-public.ts, release.ts, test-sync-local.ts)\n- [ ] Phase 4: Update .gitignore\n- [ ] Phase 5: Update standard-operating-procedures.md\n- [ ] Verify all checks pass (Step 4)\n- [ ] Implement approved optional items (Step 5)\n- [ ] Run `bun test` and log to file (Step 6)\n- [ ] Stage changes and commit (Step 7)\n- [ ] Run release dry-run post-commit (Step 7)\n- [ ] Push and create PR (Step 8)\n- [ ] Update CHANGELOG.md (Step 9)\n- [ ] Document post-merge actions for the human (Step 10)\n","structuredPatch":[],"originalFile":null},"timestamp":"2026-03-05T14:10:59.899Z"}
